abstract: >
  TriadicFrameworks defines a unified substrate for representing structure,
  relation, and transformation across mathematics, physics, computation,
  cognition, and symbolic systems. It is built on Resonance-Time Theory (RTT),
  a primitive triadic structure (pos / Q / neg), and the Vector-Space of Time
  (vST), a dimensional substrate spanning spatial, transformational, spectral,
  temporal, combinatorial, and logical modes. This repository contains the
  canonical definitions, documentation, and cross-domain modules, including a
  substrate-first reconstruction of mathematics.

